# C++ Naming Conventions
## 1. Prefixes & Namespaces
- **C++ Classes:** Always prefix class names with `JoA_` (e.g., `UJoA_UnitComponent`, `AJoA_Hero`), unless it is defined differently in @gas.mdc.
- **Enums & Structs:** Never use project prefixes like `JoA_` or `JoA_Arena` (e.g., use `EMyEnum`, NOT `JoA_EMyEnum` or `JoA_EMyStruct`).

## 2. Contextual Naming
- For Enums and Structs, name them descriptive to their context (e.g., use `EUnitType` for unit type enumerations, `FDamageInfo` for damage data).

## 3. Unreal Engine Standard Rules
- Standard Unreal Engine prefixes strictly apply:
  - `A` for Actors (e.g., `AJoA_Character`)
  - `U` for UObjects / Components (e.g., `UJoA_InventoryComponent`)
  - `F` for pure C++ structs (e.g., `FCharacterAttributes`)
  - `E` for Enums (e.g., `EUnitState`)

## 4. Widgets (UMG C++ classes)
- A widget class always uses the prefix `JoA_W_`, then the Blueprint name with its `WBP_` prefix removed.
- Keep the `U` prefix of Unreal Engine in front of the class name.
- The Blueprint `WBP_Play` gives `UJoA_W_Play`. The Blueprint `WBP_CharacterStat` gives `UJoA_W_CharacterStat`.
- The file name is the class name without the `U`: `JoA_W_Play.h` and `JoA_W_Play.cpp`.
- A widget without a Blueprint yet takes the name the Blueprint will get, with `WBP_` removed.
- This rule replaces the plain `JoA_` prefix from section 1 for widgets. It does not apply to `JoA_GAS_` classes.

# Local names must not hide members
- Never declare a local variable, parameter, or lambda capture with the same name as a member of the current class or any base class.
- Unreal builds this as error C4458. A matching name on `AActor`, `APawn`, `AController`, or `APlayerState` is enough to fail the compile.
- Name the local after its role. `PlayerState` hides `APawn::PlayerState` and `AController::PlayerState`. Use `OwnerState` for an `AJoA_PlayerState*`.
- The same rule covers inherited names such as `Owner`, `Controller`, `Instigator`, and `RootComponent`.

```cpp
// Hides APawn::PlayerState. Error C4458.
AJoA_PlayerState* PlayerState = nullptr;

// Role name. Does not hide the inherited member.
AJoA_PlayerState* OwnerState = nullptr;
```

# Renames follow the class
- When a class is renamed, rename every member of that type in other classes.
- Rename the Get and Set functions for that member to the same name.
- `UJoA_GAS_CombatSet` uses `CombatSet`, `GetCombatSet`, and `SetCombatSet`.

# Renames that leave references
- Do not add `ClassRedirects`, `ObjectRedirects`, `PropertyRedirects`, or `EnumRedirects` to `Config/DefaultEngine.ini`.
- Tell the user the old name, the new name, and which assets still store the old name. Then give the steps for that kind of rename.

## Asset moved or renamed in Content
- Right-click the folder in the Content Browser and run Update Redirector References.
- That command loads `UObjectRedirector` assets in the folder, resaves referencers onto the new asset, and can delete the redirectors.
- Save the packages it dirties.

## C++ class, property, struct, enum, or component name
- Update Redirector References finds nothing. A C++ rename does not create a redirector asset.
- Recompile and restart the editor.
- Open each Blueprint that still uses the old name. Delete the broken component or rewire the broken pin, then Compile and Save.
- If the Blueprint parent class itself was renamed, the asset will not open. Say so and ask before adding a `ClassRedirect`.

# Sound file names
When the user writes `check sound`, rename every
file in `Content/Audio/SFX/`.

- Take the file name without the extension.
- If it already starts with `SFX_`, the name is
  the rest. Otherwise the name is the whole stem.
- The new stem is `SFX_` plus that name with its
  first letter capitalized.
- `cheer` becomes `SFX_Cheer`. `SFX_Jump` stays
  `SFX_Jump`.
- Rename the source file and the `.uasset` of the
  same stem together.
- Skip a file that already has that name.
- Put the renames on the numbered CL of this work.
  Do not submit.

# Cursor rule file names
- A new rule in `.cursor/rules/` uses camelCase: `nameName.mdc`.
- `binaryGraphicsWorkflow.mdc` is right. `binary-graphics-workflow.mdc` is wrong.
- One word stays one word: `naming.mdc`, `gas.mdc`.
